<section style="padding-top:20px;">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
    <p style="font-size:1.02rem;">In Antalya, the possibilities go far beyond the beach. Whether you're drawn to the region's <strong>ancient history</strong>, eager to wander the <strong>Roman-era old town</strong>, or looking for a rafting trip through a limestone canyon, there's something here for every kind of traveler. Here's just a glimpse of what's waiting for you along Turkey's Turquoise Coast.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">

    <div class="editorial-block">
      <img src="/images/photos/things-to-do-cover.jpg" alt="Aspendos Theatre near Antalya">
      <div>
        <h3>Ancient Ruins &amp; History</h3>
        <p>The Antalya region holds some of the best-preserved Roman and Hellenistic sites anywhere in the Mediterranean. <strong>Aspendos Theatre</strong>, built in 155 AD, still has its original acoustics and hosts an opera and ballet festival every summer. A short drive further inland, <strong>Perge</strong> unveils a full Roman street grid, a stadium and a colonnaded avenue, while the hilltop ruins of <strong>Termessos</strong> — never conquered by Alexander the Great — sit inside a national park with sweeping mountain views.</p>
        <p>Closer to the coast, <strong>Side</strong> combines an active fishing harbor with a Temple of Apollo that lights up gold at sunset — one of the most photographed ruins on the entire coast.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="editorial-block">
      <img src="/images/photos/antalya-coastline.jpg" alt="Kaleiçi old town, Antalya">
      <div>
        <h3>Old Town &amp; Culture</h3>
        <p><strong>Kaleiçi</strong>, Antalya's walled old town, is built around a small working harbor that the Romans first fortified. Its narrow cobblestone lanes are lined with restored Ottoman and Greek houses, many now boutique hotels and cafés. Don't miss the fluted <strong>Yivli Minare</strong>, a 13th-century Seljuk landmark visible from most of the old town, or an afternoon spent wandering the covered bazaar streets for leather goods, ceramics and Turkish tea.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="editorial-block">
      <img src="/images/photos/manavgat-waterfall.jpg" alt="Manavgat Waterfall near Antalya">
      <div>
        <h3>Beaches &amp; Nature</h3>
        <p>Antalya offers outdoor adventurers a striking mix of mountains and coastline. <strong>Konyaaltı Beach</strong> runs along the city center itself, with the Taurus Mountains rising directly behind it. Further west, the cove at <strong>Kaputaş Beach</strong> is reached by a dramatic staircase cut into the cliffs. Inland, cool off at <strong>Manavgat Waterfall</strong> or the cliff-diving <strong>Düden Waterfalls</strong>, which drop straight into the Mediterranean at Lara.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="editorial-block">
      <img src="/images/photos/coastal-extra-1.jpg" alt="Köprülü Canyon rafting near Antalya">
      <div>
        <h3>Adventure &amp; Outdoor</h3>
        <p>For something more active, <strong>Köprülü Canyon</strong> is one of Turkey's most popular white-water rafting spots, with a national park and a Roman bridge still standing over the river. Boat tours out of Kaleiçi's harbor run daily along the coastline, and several operators offer jeep safaris into the Taurus foothills for those who want to see the region from above the tree line.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="editorial-block">
      <img src="/images/photos/generic-cover.webp" alt="Nightlife in Antalya">
      <div>
        <h3>Nightlife &amp; Entertainment</h3>
        <p>After dark, Kaleiçi's harbor-facing bars and rooftop lounges are the center of gravity, with live music spilling into the street most summer nights. Along the coast, seasonal beach clubs in Lara and Konyaaltı run through the afternoon and into the evening with DJ sets and sea views.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ EXPLORE THINGS TO DO (horizontal listing, CMS-driven) ============ -->
<section class="tint">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Explore</span>
        <h2>Explore Things to Do in Antalya</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="filter-bar">
      <span class="filter-pill">Old Town</span>
      <span class="filter-pill">Nature</span>
      <span class="filter-pill">Ancient Ruins</span>
      <span class="filter-pill">Beaches</span>
      <span class="filter-pill">Nightlife</span>
    </div>
